{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.protonExample.archimedean_agreement","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.protonExample.archimedean_agreement","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.protonExample.specialises","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.protonExample.specialises","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroResidueSumEquivalence/protonExample/archimedean_agreement.lean#L76-L87","doc":"**The proton case follows from the generic conjecture.**\n\nThe block says the proton identity *\"specializes the generic archimedean\nagreement to the proton\"*; this is that sentence, checked. It is a genuine\nderivation rather than a restatement — the generic class is quantified over\nbraids and this one is not, so the two statements differ and one implies the\nother. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.protonExample.archimedean_agreement.agree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.protonExample.archimedean_agreement.agree","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroResidueSumEquivalence/protonExample/archimedean_agreement.lean#L63-L63","doc":"**The conjecture**, at the proton braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.protonExample.archimedean_agreement.tolerance_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.protonExample.archimedean_agreement.tolerance_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroResidueSumEquivalence/protonExample/archimedean_agreement.lean#L61-L61","doc":"The tolerance is a tolerance: a negative `ε` would make the class empty\nrather than open, which is a different and wrong claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.protonExample.archimedean_agreement.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.protonExample.archimedean_agreement.mk","kind":"ctor","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroResidueSumEquivalence/protonExample/archimedean_agreement.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.protonExample.archimedean_agreement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.protonExample.archimedean_agreement","kind":"class","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroResidueSumEquivalence/protonExample/archimedean_agreement.lean#L49-L63","doc":"**Archimedean agreement (proton instance)**: the proton's degree-48\nMarkov-normalised Habiro trace, evaluated at `u₀`, agrees with the proton\nGröbner–Shirshov mass within `ε`.\n\nConjectural class — see\n[`conj:gs-archimedean-agreement-residue`](../../../../mass-theory/gs-archimedean-agreement-residue.md).\n\nParameters are the caller's data: the two evaluated quantities and the certified\ntolerance. An instance **is** the conjecture, for that data. None is provided. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:gs-archimedean-agreement-residue","label":"conj:gs-archimedean-agreement-residue","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gs-archimedean-agreement-residue.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}